1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,860
Cat can stare at a wall for forty minutes.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:05,220
Cat can watch one bird through
a window without blinking once.

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:09,820
Cat can sit inside a cardboard box that
is objectively too small, and stay there

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,880
until the box gives up.

5
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,140
Cat has patience.

6
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,400
Cat has focus.

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:17,540
Cat has, by any reasonable measure,
an excellent attention span.

8
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:21,180
But turn on a laser pointer, and Cat
becomes a completely different animal.

9
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,020
Cat sprints.

10
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:24,080
Cat skids into the leg of the table.

11
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,220
Cat knocks a glass onto the
floor without even looking at it.

12
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,820
The glass is not the point.

13
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:31,000
Nothing is the point except the dot.

14
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,220
Then the light switches off.

15
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,200
Cat stands in the middle of the room.

16
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,220
Paws empty.

17
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,420
Staring at the carpet
where the dot used to be.

18
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,480
Cat caught nothing.

19
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:39,900
Cat got nothing.

20
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:42,540
Cat will do exactly the
same thing tomorrow.

21
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:44,560
Here is the part that should bother you.

22
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,080
Cat is not stupid.

23
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,580
Cat has hunted real
things and caught them.

24
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:52,380
Cat knows the difference between a mouse
and a wall, between a moth and a shadow.

25
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,480
Every instinct Cat owns was tuned over
millions of years to be extremely good

26
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,440
at exactly this.

27
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,100
And a five dollar plastic
tube beats all of it.

28
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,340
Every single time.

29
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,820
In under two seconds.

30
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,460
So why does Cat chase something
that can never be caught?

31
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:09,400
Why does the empty ending never teach
Cat anything, no matter how many times

32
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:09,900
it happens?

33
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:13,240
And the real question, the one
this whole video is actually about.

34
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:16,400
If a dot can do that to Cat,
what is the dot in your life?

35
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,100
Part one.

36
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,920
Wanting is not liking.

37
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:21,680
Most people think the brain
has one system for pleasure.

38
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:22,580
One dial.

39
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,140
Turn it up, feel good.

40
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,720
Turn it down, feel bad.

41
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:26,600
It has two.

42
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,500
And they are not the same machine.

43
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:29,980
Liking is the part that enjoys.

44
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:31,720
Warm sunlight on the floor.

45
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:32,840
A full bowl.

46
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,200
The three seconds after
a really good stretch.

47
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:36,660
Liking is quiet.

48
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:38,240
It happens in the present.

49
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,860
It is genuinely satisfying.

50
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,740
Wanting is the part that chases.

51
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:44,040
Wanting does not care
whether the thing is good.

52
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,540
Wanting does not check.

53
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:49,580
Wanting registers one fact only:
that the thing is not here yet.

54
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,000
Dopamine is usually called
the pleasure chemical.

55
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,180
That is wrong.

56
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:57,420
And the mistake is not small, because
it points at the wrong problem entirely.

57
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,340
Dopamine is the wanting chemical.

58
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,140
It does not pay Cat for catching.

59
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,640
It pays Cat for chasing.

60
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:05,740
Which is why a red dot is
not a bad imitation of prey.

61
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,060
It is a better one.

62
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:08,560
Real prey has a flaw.

63
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,220
Real prey gets caught.

64
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,420
A mouse ends.

65
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:15,780
And when it ends, the wanting system
finally goes quiet, because it got the one

66
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,200
thing it was built to produce.

67
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,340
A finished hunt.

68
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:19,700
The dot never ends.

69
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,020
No body to catch.

70
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,300
No weight to carry.

71
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,920
No moment where Cat can
sit back and feel done.

72
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,800
It is pure chase with the
ending surgically removed.

73
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,100
Keep that word in mind.

74
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,120
Ended.

75
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:33,120
It comes back later, and it turns
out to be the entire solution.

76
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:33,800
Part two.

77
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:36,120
The rats that starved next to food.

78
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:39,720
At the University of Michigan, two
researchers pulled these two systems apart.

79
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,640
Kent Berridge and Terry Robinson.

80
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:46,120
They spent years on it, and what they
found is the reason we can talk about any

81
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:46,740
of this at all.

82
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,180
They took rats and shut
down the dopamine system.

83
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,340
Now, if dopamine were pleasure,
the prediction is obvious.

84
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,480
Those rats should stop enjoying things.

85
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,100
Food should go boring.

86
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,500
That is not what happened.

87
00:02:57,660 --> 00:03:01,240
Put something sweet on their tongue and
they made the same contented face a rat

88
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:02,300
makes for something delicious.

89
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:03,540
Same reaction.

90
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:04,620
Same intensity.

91
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,400
The liking was completely,
measurably intact.

92
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,400
But the wanting was gone.

93
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,400
Completely gone.

94
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,460
The rats would not
cross the cage for food.

95
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:14,260
They would not press a lever for it.

96
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,660
They would not work for
it in any way at all.

97
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:19,740
Some sat directly beside a
full bowl and did nothing.

98
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:22,600
Nothing in them was generating
the impulse to go and get it.

99
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:23,920
They still enjoyed food.

100
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,680
They just no longer wanted it.

101
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:29,060
And without wanting, enjoying
does not make anything move.

102
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:32,360
Then Berridge ran it the other way and
turned the wanting system up instead.

103
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,820
Those rats chased harder.

104
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:34,860
Worked longer.

105
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,380
Pushed through obstacles that
should have stopped them.

106
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,540
And here is the finding that matters most.

107
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,400
They did not enjoy the
reward any more than before.

108
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,860
Not one bit.

109
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:46,960
The pleasure stayed flat while
the pursuit went through the roof.

110
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:47,600
Part three.

111
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:49,740
Everything is a red dot now.

112
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,760
Here is where this stops being about cats.

113
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,040
Look at what is actually on the phone.

114
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,700
The feed does not end.

115
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,840
It cannot end.

116
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,140
It was specifically engineered not to end.

117
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:03,220
The video autoplays into the next one before
the last frame of this one has finished.

118
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:06,920
The notification arrives before Cat has
dealt with the previous notification.

119
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,080
Not one of those things
is designed to be caught.

120
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:13,400
Every single one of them is a dot, moving
just fast enough to stay ahead of Cat,

121
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:13,960
forever.

122
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:17,120
And Cat's wanting system does
exactly what it always did.

123
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:18,000
It fires.

124
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,060
It says go.

125
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:23,140
It has no mechanism for noticing that
this particular light will never land.

126
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,780
It never had to develop one.

127
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,400
So Cat scrolls.

128
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,600
And here is the part nobody says out loud.

129
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,480
Cat is not losing an evening.

130
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:33,600
Cat is losing the ability
to want anything slowly.

131
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:37,520
Every hour spent chasing something
engineered never to be caught teaches the

132
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,960
wanting system one lesson.

133
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,620
Reward is instant.

134
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:42,260
Reward is effortless.

135
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,760
Reward is infinite.

136
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:47,200
And a system that has learned that
stops responding to anything else.

137
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:49,600
So Cat sits down to do something real.

138
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:52,320
Something that pays out in
weeks instead of seconds.

139
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,000
And it does not feel hard.

140
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:56,080
That is the thing people
get wrong about this.

141
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,400
It does not feel hard.

142
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,020
It feels like nothing at all.

143
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,360
The signal is still there.

144
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,600
It is just too quiet to hear anymore.

145
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,100
That is the actual cost.

146
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,360
Not the time.

147
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:06,260
The volume.

148
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,300
Cat does not need less dopamine.

149
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,540
Cat needs the chase to end somewhere.

150
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:11,220
Part four.

151
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,860
Giving the dot a body.

152
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:13,520
Step one.

153
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:15,500
Let Cat catch something small.

154
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,980
Every hunt has to end in a catch,
or the system learns nothing.

155
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:21,700
So Cat finishes exactly one thing a day.

156
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:22,860
Not a project.

157
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:23,920
Not a goal.

158
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,280
One finished thing.

159
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,980
One pan washed and put away.

160
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,800
One message actually sent.

161
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:30,400
One page written badly.

162
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:34,280
The size genuinely does not matter, and
that is the part Cat kept getting wrong.

163
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:38,120
What matters is that it ends, and that
Cat is standing there when it ends.

164
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:38,860
Step two.

165
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,280
Delete the apps.

166
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,500
Cat tried this one.

167
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,920
Cat deleted everything
on a Sunday afternoon.

168
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:47,680
Felt absolutely magnificent
about it for roughly nine hours.

169
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,180
Had all of it reinstalled
by Tuesday evening.

170
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,860
Because nothing replaced it.

171
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:54,840
A cat with nothing to hunt
does not become a calm cat.

172
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:57,360
A cat with nothing to
hunt hunts the curtains.

173
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,480
Then the ankles.

174
00:05:58,700 --> 00:05:59,900
Then the plastic bag.

175
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,160
Then it finds its way back to the dot.

176
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:04,720
Removing the chase does
not remove the wanting.

177
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:07,000
It leaves it circling with nowhere to go.

178
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,580
So Cat changed the rule.

179
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:09,500
Not delete.

180
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:10,560
Replace.

181
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:14,380
Every dot that gets removed has to be
swapped for something with a real ending.

182
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,160
A walk with an actual destination.

183
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,920
A recipe with a last step.

184
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,380
A book with a final page.

185
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:22,040
The wanting system does
not need to be shut down.

186
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:24,200
It needs to be pointed at
something that finishes.

187
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:25,040
Step three.

188
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,080
Put the reward behind the work.

189
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,480
Cat used to check the phone first thing
in the morning and then try to work.

190
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,040
It never once worked.

191
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:34,780
Cat blamed discipline
for about four years.

192
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,140
It was never discipline.

193
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:38,520
The wanting system was already spent.

194
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:42,020
Cat had run the entire hunt before
breakfast and caught nothing.

195
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:45,020
Then asked an empty system
to go do something difficult.

196
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:46,380
Now the phone comes after.

197
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:47,780
Not as a punishment.

198
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,940
As the catch.

199
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:49,920
Step four.

200
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,720
Sit through the boredom.

201
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:55,600
This is the one that hurts, and Cat wants
to be honest about it rather than sell

202
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:55,920
it.

203
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:58,460
When the dots stop, what
arrives is not peace.

204
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:01,360
What arrives is a flat,
itchy stretch of time.

205
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:02,640
Nothing is interesting.

206
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,080
Nothing sounds good.

207
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:07,300
Cat wants to claw the sofa
purely to make something happen.

208
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,860
That feeling is not a
sign that this is failing.

209
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:13,180
That feeling is the wanting
system turning its volume back up.

210
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:15,620
It cannot do that while
it is still being fed.

211
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,720
The discomfort is the recalibration.

212
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,660
There is no version of
this where Cat skips it.

213
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,300
The dot was never the problem.

214
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,060
A cat that chases is a cat
that is working correctly.

215
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:29,760
The chase is the reason Cat survived, the
reason Cat learns anything, the reason

216
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:31,340
Cat gets off the sofa at all.

217
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:32,960
Wanting is not a bug.

218
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:34,600
Wanting is the engine.

219
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:36,820
So the goal was never to want less.

220
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:39,280
A cat that wants nothing
is not enlightened.

221
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:42,240
A cat that wants nothing is
the rat next to the full bowl.

222
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,960
Perfectly able to enjoy it.

223
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,660
Completely unable to move.

224
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,760
So, next time the light comes on.

225
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,540
Cat does not need more discipline.

226
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,120
Cat does not need guilt.

227
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:53,880
Cat needs to look at the
dot and ask one question.

228
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:54,940
Where does this end?

229
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:59,040
And if the honest answer is
nowhere, then Cat is not hunting.

230
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,400
Cat is being hunted.

231
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:04,980
Next time, Cat finds out why doing nothing
all day is more exhausting than doing

232
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:05,380
something.

233
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,600
The Cat says thanks.

234
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,860
Like this video?

235
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:09,180
Toss him a treat.

236
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,560
It keeps the dots moving.
